<!doctype HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd">
<!--#include file="helpVar.asp"-->
<HTML>
<HEAD>
   <TITLE>
      <%=sModel%>
      Navigation Help </TITLE>
   <META http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1">
   <LINK href="helpStyle.css" rel="stylesheet" title="WebEnabled" type="text/css">
</HEAD>
<BODY>
   <TABLE width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
      <!-- Begin logos row - middle logo is instrument specific -->
      <TR bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
         <TD valign="MIDDLE" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="230" height="60">
            <IMG src="../image/agilent.gif" width="230" height="60" border="0" alt="Agilent">
         </TD>
         <TD valign="top" bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" height="60">
            <IMG src="../image/instrumentBanner.gif" alt=""></TD>
      </TR>
      <!-- End logos row -->
      <TR>
         <TD colspan="2" bgcolor="#336699" class="blue">
            <IMG src="../image/filltrans.gif" height="2" alt=""></TD>
      </TR>
   </TABLE>
   <H1>
      Navigation Tab Help</H1>
   <UL>
      <LI>Welcome Page
         <BR>
         The Welcome Page displays the basic information about the
         <%=sModel%>
         &nbsp;oscilloscope.
         <BR>
      </LI>
      <LI>Browser Web Control<BR>
         The Browser Web Control page provides methods to control the instrument using
      menus and SCPI&nbsp;commands.
      <LI>Get Image<BR>
         The Get Image page provides a high resolution image of the instrument screen.
      The image is in PNG format and can be copied from the browser into other applications.
      <LI>Instrument Utilities
         <BR>
         The Instrument Utilities pages show installed options, calibration status, firmware
         version information and provides a means to upgrade the
         <%=sModel%>.
         <BR>
      </LI>
      <LI>Configure Network
         <BR>
         The Configure Network pages show the current configuration and allows access to
         the Modify Configuration page. The Modify Configuration page allows you to change
         LAN and GPIB settings of the
         <%=sModel%>
         &nbsp;and a means to set password protection.
         <BR>
      </LI>
      <LI>Print Page
         <BR>
         The Print Page allows you to print a copy of the current page. To use this button,
         your browser must be set up with a printer function.<BR>
      </LI>
      <LI>Help with this Page
         <BR>
         Help with this Page provides context sensitive guidance on configuration of the
         <%=sModel%>. 
      </LI>
   </UL>
</BODY>
</HTML>
